# Ōzakura pilot v2 — Prologue + Chapter 1 (source script)
# Compiled by production/pipeline/vn/compile_script.py into v2/script.json and the voice job list.
#
# Syntax
#   == scene_id | Dev-chart title
#   > narration
#   who: "English" || 日本語            spoken line (日本語 is what gets voiced; "-" = unvoiced)
#   who<expr>: ...                      change that character's sprite expression first (outfit kept)
#   kohei(face): ...                    Kōhei's face-window expression
#   who(expr): ...                      any speaker shown only in a face window (e.g. an interlude's POV character)
#   @show who outfit_expr pos  @hide who  @hideall  @move who pos
#   @bg name [cut|fade|slow]  @cg name [cut|fade|slow]  @cg -
#   @bgm name  @bgm -   @sfx name   @wait seconds   @flash white
#   @card text   @chapter n | title   @mode interlude Label   @mode normal   @endchapter n
#   {term|gloss}  Japanese term shown with a small English gloss (style guide §5)
#
# Names in the Japanese lines are in kana until their kanji are chosen (pilot-notes fix 14).

== prologue | The Dream
@bg black cut
@bgm memory
@wait 0.7
> There's a dream I've had since I was small.
> I never remember it properly when I wake. Only pieces.
@cg cg_dream slow
> The sound of a river, close by.
> My wrist stings. There's a cut on the inside of it from training, and I've held it closed the whole way home.
> Somewhere above us, a branch moving in the wind.
> Petals.
past_natsuki: "You're late." || ……遅いですよ。
> She says it like a scolding. She says it like she's laughing.
> She says it like she's been waiting a very long time.
past_natsuki: "Hurt again. Give me your hand… Hold still." || また怪我して。……手、見せてください。じっとして。
> Hands that aren't mine wind a strip of cloth around a wrist that is. Slow and careful, like the knot matters more than anything else in the world.
@flash white
> And then I wake up, and the only thing left is a feeling I can't put a name to.
> That someone was waiting for me.
> That I kept them waiting far too long.
@bgm -
@bg black slow
@wait 1.0
@chapter 1 | The House Next Door

== c1_morning | Mornings at the Fujisawas
@card Monday, April 7
@bg bg_kohei_room_day
@bgm daily
> My alarm goes off at 5:40.
> I'm usually awake before it. I lie there for the full ten seconds anyway, as a matter of principle, listening to the house.
> The water heater ticking. A crow on the power line. Nothing from the room down the hall.
> Second year of high school starts today. It doesn't feel like anything starts. It feels like Monday.
> I get up.
@bg bg_fujisawa_kitchen
> The rice was on the timer last night, so the kitchen already smells like steam. Eggs, the leftover spinach, the last of the frozen karaage. Two lunch boxes, side by side on the counter.
> I've gotten fast at this. Fast enough to do it while reading the calendar on the wall.
> Kendo: Monday, Wednesday, Friday and Saturday morning. Hoshino Kitchen: Tuesday, Thursday and Sunday. A red circle around the eighteenth, Akane's clinic day. All of it in my handwriting.
> All of it except the bottom line, which still says "Garbage: burnables, Mon/Thu" in Dad's. He wrote it last spring. I've never written over it.
> The fusuma to Mom's room is closed. It usually is.
@wait 0.6
@show akane school_sleepy c
akane: "Morning, Onii-chan…" || おはよ、お兄ちゃん……
> My sister shuffles in already dressed for school, eyes still at half-mast.
kohei(smile): "Morning. How'd you sleep?" || おはよう。よく眠れたか？
akane<pout>: "You asked me that yesterday." || それ、昨日も聞いた。
kohei(deadpan): "And?" || で？
akane<tease>: "And I slept yesterday too. Two nights in a row. Medical science is baffled." || 昨日もちゃんと寝たよ。二晩連続。医学界もびっくりだね。
> I look at her anyway. Color's fine. She isn't leaning on the doorframe. She isn't holding her head the way she does when the room starts tilting on her.
akane<pout>: "Stop doing the face." || その顔、やめて。
kohei(neutral): "What face?" || どの顔だよ。
akane<tease>: "The doctor face. You don't have a license, Onii-chan." || お医者さんの顔。お兄ちゃん、免許持ってないでしょ。
kohei(smile): "I've got an egg with your name on it. That's basically a license." || お前の名前入りの卵焼きがある。ほぼ免許だろ。
akane<smile>: "I could make my own lunch, you know. I'm very talented." || お弁当くらい、自分で作れるよ？ 私、けっこう器用なんだから。
kohei(smile): "I'm already making two." || どうせ二つ作ってるし。
akane<pout>: "…That's sort of my point." || ……そういうとこだよ、お兄ちゃん。
> She says it to the rice cooker, not to me. I pretend I didn't hear that.
@sfx door_slide
> The back door slides open. No knock. There's never a knock.
@move akane l
@show nanoha school_smile r
nanoha: "Good morning. I'm coming in." || おはよう。おじゃましまーす。
kohei(deadpan): "You're already in." || もう入ってるだろ。
nanoha<happy>: "Then I've arrived. Good morning, Akane-chan." || じゃあ、到着しました。おはよう、あかねちゃん。
akane<happy>: "Morning, Nanoha-chan!" || おはよ、なのはちゃん！
> She sets a plastic container on the table.
nanoha<smile>: "Kinpira. Mom made too much again." || きんぴら。お母さんが、また作りすぎちゃって。
kohei(neutral): "Again." || また、か。
nanoha<deadpan>: "Again. She's very bad at measuring burdock. It's a sickness." || また。ごぼうを量るのが、ほんとに苦手なの。もう病気だね。
> She's been bringing food over for about a year now. I used to argue. Somewhere around last summer, I gave up.
kohei(smile): "Tell her thanks." || おばさんに、ありがとうって伝えといて。
nanoha<smile>: "I'll tell her you said it like you meant it." || 心を込めて言ってたって、伝えておくね。
> She goes to the cupboard left of the sink, the one with the mugs and not the one with the glasses, and takes down two without looking. She bumps the drawer under the counter with her hip so it won't stick. She reaches over the sink and jiggles the window latch at the exact angle it needs, so the steam can get out.
> She's been doing all of that since she was tall enough to reach.
> Which, considering it's Nanoha, wasn't that long ago.
nanoha<deadpan>: "I heard that." || 聞こえたよ。
kohei(surprised): "I didn't say anything." || 何も言ってないだろ。
nanoha<deadpan>: "You thought it in a short-person direction." || 背が低い方向のこと、考えてたでしょ。
akane<tease>: "He did. I saw his face." || 考えてたよ。顔に出てた。
kohei(annoyed): "Whose side are you on?" || お前、どっちの味方なんだよ。
akane<happy>: "Hers. She brought kinpira." || なのはちゃん。きんぴら持ってきてくれたもん。
@hideall
> I wrap the lunches. I knock twice on the fusuma.
kohei(neutral): "Mom, we're heading out. There's rice in the cooker and miso on the stove. Just heat it up." || 母さん、行ってくる。ご飯は炊飯器、味噌汁はコンロにあるから。温めて食べて。
> Nothing.
> Then a small shift of weight on the other side of the paper. A creak of floorboard.
> That's an answer. Sort of.

== c1_river | The river walk
@bg bg_river_morning
@bgm nanoha
> The path to school follows the river for a while before it turns toward town.
> This week it's the best walk in Shirasawa. The cherry trees along the embankment are in full bloom, so heavy with flowers the branches sag over the path, and every time the wind comes down off the mountains the whole tunnel lets go at once.
@show nanoha school_smile c
> Nanoha walks on the river side. She always walks on the river side. I don't remember when we decided that.
nanoha: "So. Class assignments." || さて。クラス分け。
kohei(neutral): "They'll be posted at the entrance." || 昇降口に貼り出されてるだろ。
nanoha<deadpan>: "That's the boring answer. I've prepared a theory." || それはつまらない答え。私は、仮説を用意してきました。
kohei(smile): "Of course you have." || だろうな。
nanoha<smile>: "There are six second-year classes. On paper, our odds of being in the same one are one in six." || 二年生は六クラス。計算上、私たちが同じクラスになる確率は、六分の一。
nanoha<tease>: "However. We've been in the same class four years running. A teacher somewhere has noticed. A file has been opened. There have been meetings." || しかし。私たちは四年連続で同じクラスです。どこかの先生が気づいてる。ファイルが作られてる。会議も、開かれてる。
kohei(deadpan): "Meetings." || 会議。
nanoha<deadpan>: "In a small room with no windows. They've realized that if we're separated, something terrible happens. The school's feng shui collapses. The pool turns green." || 窓のない小さな部屋で。私たちを離すと、恐ろしいことが起きるって気づいたの。学校の風水が崩れて、プールが緑色になる。
kohei(deadpan): "The pool is green." || プールは緑だぞ。
nanoha<deadpan>: "Because last year they put you in 1-C for five days during the exchange program. You remember." || 去年、交流プログラムの間、こうへいを五日間だけ一年C組にしたからだよ。覚えてるでしょ。
kohei(smile): "That was a scheduling error." || あれは日程のミスだって。
nanoha<deadpan>: "That's what they want you to think." || ……そう思わされてるだけ。
> I laugh. I can't help it.
nanoha<happy>: "You laughed. That's two points for me this morning." || 笑った。今朝はこれで、私に二ポイント。
kohei(grin): "We're keeping score now?" || 点数つけてたのかよ。
nanoha<smile>: "We've always been keeping score. You're losing." || ずっとつけてるよ。こうへいの負け越し。
> A gust shakes the trees. Petals come down so thick it's like walking through snow that forgot to be cold. One lands in her hair, right on the clip, and stays there.
> I don't mention it. It suits her.
nanoha<deadpan>: "Kō-chan. Your collar." || こうちゃん。襟。
@cg cg_collar
> Before I can do anything about it, she's stopped in front of me, up on her toes, folding my shirt collar back down over my tie.
> She has to stretch to reach. She's always had to stretch to reach.
> Her hands stay a second longer than the collar strictly needs.
> Probably a stubborn crease.
nanoha<smile>: "There. Now you look like someone who has his life together." || はい、できた。これで、人生ちゃんとしてる人に見えるよ。
@cg -
kohei(smile): "Looks can be deceiving." || 見た目にだまされるなよ。
nanoha<tease>: "That's why I fix them." || だから、私が直すの。
> We walk on. A bike bell rings somewhere behind us and doesn't pass.
nanoha<smile>: "Practice today?" || 今日、部活？
kohei(neutral): "Club doesn't start until Wednesday. First week." || 部活は水曜から。最初の週だし。
nanoha<smile>: "And after that?" || そのあとは？
kohei(neutral): "Monday, Wednesday, Friday, Saturday morning. Shifts Tuesday, Thursday, Sunday." || 月、水、金、土曜の朝。バイトが火曜、木曜、日曜。
nanoha<sad>: "I know." || ……知ってる。
kohei(surprised): "Then why'd you ask?" || じゃあ、なんで聞いたんだよ。
nanoha<sad>: "So you'd hear yourself say it." || 自分で言ってるの、聞いてほしかったから。
> She doesn't say it like a criticism. She says it like a weather report. That's somehow worse.
kohei(smile): "It's fine. I like being busy." || 平気だって。忙しいの、嫌いじゃないし。
nanoha<smile>: "Mm." || ……うん。
> A few steps of nothing. The river is loud this time of year, fat with snowmelt from the Tanzawa.
nanoha<happy>: "Oh. Grandpa says the Ōzakura's the best it's been in years. I'm helping him sweep up there Saturday." || あ。おじいちゃんがね、今年の大桜は、何年かぶりの見頃なんだって。土曜日、上の神社の掃除を手伝うの。
kohei(neutral): "His back again?" || また腰か？
nanoha<deadpan>: "His back is a very convenient back. It only hurts on days with a lot of petals." || おじいちゃんの腰は、すごく都合のいい腰なの。花びらの多い日だけ痛くなるんだよ。
kohei(smile): "I'll come after practice. Somebody has to carry the trash bags while you supervise." || 部活のあとで行くよ。お前が監督してる間、誰かがゴミ袋運ばないとな。
nanoha<happy>: "I do supervise beautifully." || 監督させたら、私は一流だからね。
> She walks a little faster after that, and for a while I actually have to work to keep up.
@hide nanoha

