nanoha<happy>: "Good morning, Rika-chan." || おはよう、りかちゃん。
> Today's clips are a strawberry, a star and a small frog wearing a crown. The frog is new.
rika<scheme>: "And Fujisawa-kun's in Two-B too. Hm. Hmmm." || で、ふじさわくんも二のBなんだ。ふーん。ふーーーん。
kohei(deadpan): "What's 'hmmm'?" || なんだよ、その「ふーん」。
rika<grin>: "Nothing! Nothing at all. A completely neutral hmmm." || なんでもない！ ぜーんぜん！ 完全に中立な「ふーん」だから！
@show ryosuke school_smug c
ryosuke: "—which is why, structurally, a hot dog is a sandwich." || ……だから構造的に言えば、ホットドッグはサンドイッチなんだよ。
> Tokiwa has arrived the way he usually does, in the middle of an argument nobody else knew had started.
kohei(deadpan): "Good morning, Tokiwa." || おはよう、ときわ。
ryosuke<neutral>: "Bread on two sides. Filling in the middle. A hinge doesn't disqualify it. A sub roll has a hinge, and nobody says a sub isn't a sandwich." || 両側にパン。真ん中に具。つながっていても失格にはならない。サブマリンサンドだってつながってるけど、誰もあれをサンドイッチじゃないとは言わない。
kohei(deadpan): "It's seven-fifty in the morning." || 朝の七時五十分だぞ。
ryosuke<smug>: "That's not a counterargument. That's a timestamp." || それは反論じゃない。ただの時刻だ。
rika<surprised>: "It's a hot DOG! It says so in the name!" || ホットドッグだよ！ 名前に書いてあるじゃん！
ryosuke<smug>: "By that logic, a pancake is a cake." || その理屈だと、ホットケーキはケーキってことになるね。
rika<scheme>: "…Isn't it?" || ……違うの？
ryosuke<sigh>: "We'll resume this at lunch. I'll need a diagram." || この続きは昼休みにしよう。図が要る。
kohei(smile): "Please don't." || やめてくれ。
ryosuke<smug>: "Also, we're all in Two-B. I've already chosen my seat." || ちなみに、全員二のBだ。席はもう決めてある。
kohei(neutral): "We haven't seen the room yet." || まだ教室も見てないだろ。
ryosuke<smug>: "I chose it theoretically. Third row, by the window, out of the teacher's natural sightline but close enough to the heater for winter." || 理論上で決めたんだよ。三列目の窓際。先生の自然な視線から外れつつ、冬はストーブに近い。
rika<scheme>: "Oh! Oh oh oh, but have you heard? Two-B is getting a transfer student!" || あっ！ あっあっあっ、ねえ聞いた？ 二のBに転校生が来るんだって！
nanoha<surprised>: "A transfer student?" || 転校生？
rika<grin>: "A girl! From somewhere! Far!" || 女の子！ どこか……遠いところから！
ryosuke<sigh>: "'Somewhere far' covers most of the planet." || 「遠いところ」って、地球のほとんどが当てはまるよ。
rika<scheme>: "Then we've already narrowed it down!" || じゃあ、もうだいぶ絞れてるじゃん！
> While they argue, I squeeze toward the board. I don't make it. Nanoha has already slipped through somewhere at elbow height and is pointing up at a line I can't see yet.
@hide ryosuke
@hide rika
@move nanoha c
@show nanoha school_smile c
nanoha: "Fujisawa Kōhei. Two-B. About halfway down." || ふじさわこうへい。二年B組。真ん中あたり。
kohei(surprised): "You found mine before yours?" || 自分のより先に、俺の見つけたのか？
nanoha<smile>: "Yours was easier. It's always right under Fukuda's. Fukuda is very easy to find." || こうへいのほうが簡単だったの。いつも、ふくだくんのすぐ下だから。ふくだくんは、すごく見つけやすい。
> When I finally get to the board, there's no Fukuda in Two-B this year. She went looking for mine before her own.
> I don't know why that's the thing that sticks with me all through the opening ceremony.
