> Nanoha's standing by my desk with her lunch held in front of her in both hands, the way she holds things when she's about to do something brave.
natsuki<surprised>: "Oh—hi. You're…" || あ、どうも。えっと、きみは……
nanoha<smile>: "Tachibana Nanoha. I sit two rows over. I was the class representative's assistant last year, so I still own a clipboard." || たちばななのはです。二列向こうの席。去年、学級委員の補佐をやってたから……今もクリップボードを持ってます。
nanoha<smile>: "If you'd like, I could show you around after school? The library, the music rooms. Which shoe lockers stick. Which vending machine eats coins. That kind of thing." || よかったら、放課後に校内を案内しようか？ 図書室とか、音楽室とか。どの下駄箱がひっかかるか。どの自販機がお金を食べるか。そういうの。
> For a second Mizuno doesn't say anything. She looks almost startled, like she isn't used to being the one who gets asked.
natsuki<blush>: "…Really? You'd do that?" || ……ほんとに？ 案内してくれるの？
nanoha<smile>: "It's not a big tour. The vending machine part is the most important." || 大したツアーじゃないよ。自販機のところが、一番大事。
natsuki<laugh>: "I would love that. Really. Thank you." || すっごく嬉しい。ほんとに。ありがとう。
natsuki<grin>: "Oh, and call me Natsuki. Is that okay? People tell me I'm pushy." || あ、それと、なつきって呼んで。いいかな？ 押しが強いって、よく言われるんだけど。
nanoha<blush>: "…Natsuki-san." || ……なつき、さん。
natsuki<surprised>: "Eh, 'san'? We're the same age!" || えー、「さん」？ 同い年じゃん！
nanoha<tease>: "I'm working up to it. I need time to adjust." || 段階を踏んでるの。慣れるのに、時間がいるから。
natsuki<smile>: "Okay, okay. Then I'll just call you Nanoha. Is that all right? I'm going to do it anyway." || わかった、わかった。じゃあ、私は「なのは」って呼ぶね。いい？ どっちにしろ呼ぶけど。
nanoha<blush>: "That's—yes. That's fine." || それは……うん。いいよ。
> They both laugh, and something about the two of them laughing in the window light, over the top of my head, makes me feel weirdly like furniture.
@hideall
> I eat my rice. It's very good rice. I made it myself.

== c1_interlude | Nanoha: the tour
@mode interlude Interlude: Nanoha
@bg bg_classroom_evening
@bgm nanoha
> Natsuki noticed everything.
> That was the first thing Nanoha learned on the tour. Natsuki noticed that the stairs by the art room squeaked on the fourth step and the eleventh. She noticed the faded rectangle on the wall where a trophy case used to be. She noticed that the third-floor girls' bathroom had a window that looked straight at the mountains, and she said "Oh," very quietly, like she'd been handed something.
> They ended the tour in their own empty classroom, the evening sun coming in sideways and turning every desk gold. Natsuki leaned back against the desk in front of her own.
@show natsuki school_smile c
natsuki: "This school's nice. It feels… lived in. Does that make sense?" || この学校、いいね。なんか……使い込まれてる感じがする。わかる？
nanoha(smile): "It's very old. The heating sounds like a ghost." || すごく古いからね。暖房の音が、おばけみたいなの。
natsuki<laugh>: "Perfect. I love it already." || 最高。もう好きになっちゃった。
natsuki<smirk>: "So. You and Fujisawa." || で。なのはと、ふじさわって。
nanoha(surprised): "Me and Kōhei?" || 私と、こうへい？
natsuki<smile>: "You live next door, right? Somebody said." || お隣さんなんでしょ？ 誰かが言ってた。
nanoha(smile): "Since we were born." || 生まれた時からね。
natsuki<surprised>: "No way. So you're real childhood friends." || うそ。じゃあ、ほんとの幼なじみなんだ。
nanoha(smile): "Real childhood friends." || ほんとの幼なじみ。
> Nanoha said it as lightly as she knew how. She'd had practice.
natsuki<wistful>: "That's really nice." || ……いいなあ、そういうの。
natsuki<wistful>: "I've never stayed anywhere long enough to have one of those. You know? Someone who knows which drawer sticks in your kitchen." || 私、そういうのができるほど、ひとつの場所にいたことないんだ。わかる？ 台所のどの引き出しがひっかかるか、知ってるような人。
> Nanoha didn't say that Kōhei's kitchen drawer stuck. She didn't say she'd known it since she was six.
natsuki<smile>: "Hey. This is going to sound weird." || ねえ。変なこと言うけど。
nanoha(smile): "I like weird." || 変なの、好きだよ。
natsuki<wistful>: "Does he ever seem like… someone you've met before?" || ふじさわってさ……前にも会ったことがあるような……そんな感じ、しない？
nanoha(surprised): "…" || -
nanoha(tease): "I have met him before. Every day. For sixteen years." || 会ったこと、あるよ。毎日。十六年間。
natsuki<laugh>: "Okay, fair! Fair. Forget it. It's the jet lag talking." || だよね！ そりゃそうだ！ 忘れて。時差ボケのせい。
nanoha(deadpan): "You moved from Sendai. That's barely three hours by train." || 仙台から来たんでしょ。電車でたった三時間くらいだよ。
natsuki<blush>: "Very intense jet lag." || すっごく強烈な時差ボケなの。
> Natsuki laughed first. The moment closed up, and it was fine.
> It was fine.
natsuki<smile>: "Thanks for today, Nanoha. Seriously. First days are usually…" || 今日はありがとね、なのは。ほんとに。転校初日って、いつもは……
> She didn't finish. She just smiled, and it was a different smile from the one she'd used in front of the class. Smaller. It looked like it cost her something.
natsuki<wistful>: "Anyway. Thanks." || ……とにかく。ありがと。
@hide natsuki
> Somewhere between the library and the gym, Nanoha had decided that she liked Mizuno Natsuki.
